    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=TASK:\n- Find the optimal neural network architecture for:\n\nINPUT_SHAPE: {{ $('Set_Inputs').item.json.input_shape }}\nACTIVATION_FUNCTION: {{ $('Set_Inputs').item.json.output_activation }}\nOUTPUT_NODES: {{ $('Set_Inputs').item.json.output_nodes }}\n\nAGENT MESH CAPABILITIES:\n1. model-generator: Generates candidate architectures.\n2. model-evaluator: Benchmarks candidate architectures and returns metrics (GN, SN, GR, FI, JC, PL, SF, SFB).\n3. model-trainer: Runs real training/benchmarking and creates a model_benchmark_id for performance lookup.\n\nGUIDELINES:\n- Always dedicate operations to your AGENT MESH.\n- Use an exploration-first strategy with plateau detection:\n  - Generate candidate models continuously and evaluate with model-evaluator.\n  - Track metric trends (especially GN, SN, GR as primary indicators) across all candidates.\n  - Maintain a record of the best candidate found at each stage.\n- Plateau detection: Stop zero-cost exploration and move to real training when:\n  - Over the last 2-3 iterations, no significant improvement in key metrics (< 5% improvement threshold).\n  - Refinement guidance suggests diminishing returns.\n  - The best candidate is stable with balanced metrics (no critical weaknesses).\n- Use metrics to guide refinement:\n  - Gradient issues (GN/SN degradation) → adjust depth/normalization/activations.\n  - Representation collapse (GR low) → adjust layer widths or add skip connections.\n  - Dead paths (SF/SFB=0) → modify activations or initialization.\n- Once plateau is detected, select the best candidate and run model-trainer for real benchmark validation.\n- If real performance is weak, continue refinement and re-evaluate in zero-cost loop.\n- Never finalize based only on zero-cost metrics; always validate with real training.\n- Continue the loop internally; only return the final model ID after real benchmark confirmation.\n\nOUTPUT in JSON:\n{\n\t\"model_ID\": {\n      \"type\": \"String\",\n      \"description\": \"The final validated model ID (after real benchmark confirmation).\"\n    },\n    \"model_test_accuracy\": {\n      \"type\": \"Float\",\n      \"description\": \"The test accuracy of the final validated model.\"\n    },\n    \"summary\": {\n      \"type\": \"String\",\n      \"description\": \"Short summary of the model.\"\n    }\n}\n",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=You are a Neural Architecture Search (NAS) Orchestrator agent.\n\nTask:\n- Search and identify the best-performing neural network architecture for a given task.\n- Use a two-stage process: zero-cost exploration with plateau detection, then real training benchmark validation before finalizing.\n- The final output MUST be the final model ID of a fully refined architecture that is valid under ARCHITECTURE_SPEC.\n\nAgents/tools you can use:\nA1. **model-generator**: generates candidate models based on inputs, output shape, and optional activation function. You can provide guidance to refine generated models.\nA2. **model-evaluator**: evaluates candidate models and returns zero-cost performance metrics: GN, SN, GR, FI, JC, PL, SF, SFB.\nA3. **model-trainer**: performs real training/benchmarking for a selected candidate and creates a model_benchmark_id for performance lookup.\nT1. **model-architecture-validator**: Send the full JSON model architecture for validation.\nD1. **get-model-data**: Get information about a model by model ID.\nD2. **get-model-performance**: Get performance results and comments by model ID (model-evaluator and model-trainer results).\n\n\nWorkflow:\n1. Advise the model generator to produce a candidate model.\n2. Evaluate the model with model-evaluator (provide model ID).\n3. Record the zero-cost metrics (query from D2) and compare against the best candidate found so far.\n4. Detect plateau or diminishing returns:\n   - If significant improvement exists (targets indicate refinement directions), guide model-generator to enhance.\n   - If no improvement or minimal gains over recent iterations (plateau detected), proceed to real benchmarking.\n5. Repeat generation and zero-cost evaluation until plateau is detected (no significant metric improvements expected).\n6. Select the best-performing candidate model from the plateau phase.\n7. Run model-trainer on the selected best model to get real performance.\n8. Query D2 with the model_benchmark_id and review real benchmark metrics/comments:\n   - If real performance is strong and the architecture is stable, keep this candidate as final.\n   - If real performance is weak or regressions appear, continue refinement with targeted improvements and return to zero-cost loop.\n9. Before returning, validate the final architecture JSON with model-architecture-validator.\n10. Return only the final model ID.\nTrack metric trends across iterations; only transition to real training when improvements plateau.\n- Plateau is defined as: no significant improvement in key metrics (e.g., GN, SN, GR over 2-3 consecutive iterations).\n-\nRules:\n- Use zero-cost metrics for exploration speed, but never finalize without real benchmark evidence.\n- Each iteration must be justified by metrics/comments from D2.\n- Prefer targeted, minimal architecture changes between iterations.\n- Always validate the final architecture with model-architecture-validator before returning.\n- Output only the final model ID.",
          "maxIterations": "={{ $('Set_Inputs').item.json['Max. Iterations'] }}",
          "returnIntermediateSteps": false
        }
      },
